WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:05.010
- This hospital is in the front lines

00:00:05.010 --> 00:00:08.673
of Brazil's fight against
the new wave of COVID-19,

00:00:08.673 --> 00:00:11.833
one that's marked by the new variant, P.1,

00:00:11.833 --> 00:00:13.420
which is more aggressive

00:00:13.420 --> 00:00:15.323
than the traditional coronavirus.

00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:20.690
The patient behind me is 22 years old.

00:00:20.690 --> 00:00:24.720
That's a new characteristic of COVID-19.

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:26.500
Here in Porto Alegre,

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:29.050
more and more young adults

00:00:29.050 --> 00:00:31.923
are coming to the ICU for treatment.

00:00:33.095 --> 00:00:38.095
(dramatic music)
(machines beeping)

00:00:39.459 --> 00:00:43.376
(speaking in foreign language)

00:00:46.495 --> 00:00:49.551
(machine beeping)

00:00:49.551 --> 00:00:52.218
(pensive music)

00:00:55.528 --> 00:00:57.880
- We don't have enough space,

00:00:57.880 --> 00:00:58.880
we don't have enough people,

00:00:58.880 --> 00:01:00.270
we don't have enough equipment,

00:01:00.270 --> 00:01:02.791
so this is very frustrating for us.

00:01:02.791 --> 00:01:07.791
(dramatic music)
(machines beeping)

00:01:11.625 --> 00:01:16.625
(pensive music)
(pen drawing)

00:01:35.890 --> 00:01:38.560
- We believe this is the consequence

00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:43.410
of the relaxation of the
mitigation strategies

00:01:43.410 --> 00:01:47.820
of social distancing, mask
wearing and hand washing

00:01:47.820 --> 00:01:51.093
and the basic measures
that we all learned.

00:01:52.012 --> 00:01:54.620
(machines beeping)

00:01:54.620 --> 00:01:56.620
- This room here has nine patients,

00:01:56.620 --> 00:01:59.150
all of them in ICU.

00:01:59.150 --> 00:02:01.900
But there isn't a lot of ICUs in town

00:02:01.900 --> 00:02:03.780
to take everybody in.

00:02:03.780 --> 00:02:07.233
So they stayed here waiting
for a spot to open somewhere.

00:02:08.920 --> 00:02:10.600
Those patients here,

00:02:10.600 --> 00:02:12.927
they have been improvised
in these semi-beds.

00:02:15.362 --> 00:02:18.067
And they're hooked up to oxygen

00:02:18.067 --> 00:02:22.440
but the hooks that are
supposed to feed one patient

00:02:23.470 --> 00:02:25.910
are feeding two or more.

00:02:25.910 --> 00:02:28.330
Here on the other side,

00:02:28.330 --> 00:02:31.520
you can see there are more
people in the same situation

00:02:32.430 --> 00:02:35.660
and the nurses and doctors here,

00:02:35.660 --> 00:02:38.350
they're doing their best to keep them safe

00:02:38.350 --> 00:02:40.272
and treat them.

00:02:40.272 --> 00:02:42.939
(pensive music)

00:02:48.131 --> 00:02:52.048
(speaking in foreign language)

00:03:08.930 --> 00:03:11.847
(machines beeping)

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:18.690
- So now we have more
people in their 30s and 40s,

00:03:18.690 --> 00:03:20.420
working age people,

00:03:20.420 --> 00:03:24.380
who spent several days here

00:03:24.380 --> 00:03:27.560
but the staff tells me

00:03:27.560 --> 00:03:30.650
that the rate of death is going up

00:03:30.650 --> 00:03:34.430
and this special new variant, P.1,

00:03:34.430 --> 00:03:38.093
they tend to deteriorate very fast.

00:03:39.296 --> 00:03:41.833
- This is extremely difficult for us.

00:03:44.210 --> 00:03:48.420
Many patients came to
the ICU severely ill.

00:03:48.420 --> 00:03:50.043
Young patients dying.

00:03:50.910 --> 00:03:54.300
It's not uncommon to see parents

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:58.590
and kids hospitalized at the same time.

00:03:58.590 --> 00:04:00.999
Dying one after the other.

00:04:00.999 --> 00:04:03.749
(dramatic music)

00:04:25.365 --> 00:04:29.282
(speaking in foreign language)

00:04:32.452 --> 00:04:35.202
(dramatic music)

00:04:38.320 --> 00:04:40.324
- The situation's getting worse.

00:04:40.324 --> 00:04:45.070
The system is above capacity

00:04:45.070 --> 00:04:49.040
and the doctors, they
estimate that the situation

00:04:49.040 --> 00:04:52.754
won't improve for the next several weeks.

00:04:52.754 --> 00:04:55.504
(dramatic music)

